From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tomaszstaniak <68373859+tomaszstaniak@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 15:39:09 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] wordcraft-cli: own stack and an ending rayon pool on AROS

Problem: an AROS program runs on its caller's stack (40,960 bytes in an
  AROS One Shell), which layout and rendering overrun; and AROS's pthread
  library joins every thread at exit, so the idle workers of rayon's global
  pool (vello_cpu renders on them) would keep a finished command from
  exiting. Both were seen with the PhotoCraft port on the same platform.
Rationale: run the command on a thread with an 8 MiB stack and join it;
  then end rayon's global pool with terminate_global_thread_pool() from the
  port's patched rayon-core 1.13.0. Same as the PhotoCraft AROS port's
  patches 0006 and 0021.
Scope: AROS only; other targets are unchanged. Cargo.lock gains rayon-core
  in wordcraft-cli's dependency list.
Upstream-status: local-only until the rayon-core change is accepted.
Prerequisites: crate patch rayon-core-1.13.0/0001.
Verification: see the port's evidence reports.
Removal: when rayon can end its global pool and AROS programs get a stack
  of their own.
---
 Cargo.lock                     |  1 +
 apps/wordcraft-cli/Cargo.toml  |  5 +++++
 apps/wordcraft-cli/src/main.rs | 25 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 30 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

